From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: bound the luminance histogram index

The histogram bin comes from the sample values, which unpacked 10/12-bit
formats hold in 16-bit containers. A frame with larger values (a capture
the receiver rejected but returned) indexed past yHistogram and
yHistogramGrid; with _GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS the bounds check aborts the
camera service. Count out-of-range samples in the top bin, as
patches/libcamera-fedora/0003 does for the desktop.

diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp
index 1ff40322..fbf2339d 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@
 
 #include "libcamera/internal/software_isp/swstats_cpu.h"
 
+#include <algorithm>
+
 #include <libcamera/base/log.h>
 
 #include <libcamera/stream.h>
@@ -224,8 +226,10 @@ static constexpr unsigned int kBlueYMul = 29; /* 0.114 * 256 */
 	yVal = r * kRedYMul;               \
 	yVal += g * kGreenYMul;            \
 	yVal += b * kBlueYMul;             \
-	const unsigned int histIndex = yVal * SwIspStats::kYHistogramSize / \
-		(256 * 256 * (div)); \
+	/* Out-of-range samples count in the top bin. */ \
+	const unsigned int histIndex = std::min<uint64_t>( \
+		yVal * SwIspStats::kYHistogramSize / (256 * 256 * (div)), \
+		SwIspStats::kYHistogramSize - 1); \
 	const unsigned int gridX = x < gridXBoundary1 ? 0 \
 		: x < gridXBoundary2 ? 1 : 2; \
 	const unsigned int gridIndex = gridY * 3 + gridX; \
